skeptic.fix:
In src/auction/ERC20EnglishAuction.sol, add a gas floor before the `try` in `_refundOutbid` (the same pattern as src/KilimAuction.sol:190):

```solidity
error InsufficientRefundGas();

function _refundOutbid(address bidder, uint256 amount) internal {
    if (bidder == address(0)) return;
    // The refund must always get its full allowance and still leave enough for the deferred path,
    // so the gas a bid needs never depends on what the outbid address does.
    if (gasleft() < REFUND_GAS + REFUND_GAS / 63 + 60_000) revert InsufficientRefundGas();
    try this.payOutbidRefund{gas: REFUND_GAS}(bidder, amount) {
        emit RefundPaid(bidder, amount);
    } catch {
        refunds[bidder] += amount;
        refundLiability += amount;
        emit RefundDeferred(bidder, amount);
    }
}
```

I tested exactly this on a scratch copy: the minimum gas became the same (334,993 execution) whether the receiver was cheap, burning, or burning then reverting, and every blocked-bid scenario went through.

The catch: every outbidding bid then needs a gas limit of about 357k even though it uses about 140k (the rest is returned). To shrink that, lower REFUND_GAS for ETH mode to 30-50k at the same time. An EOA needs none and a Safe needs under 10k; a wallet with a heavier `receive()` simply falls back to `withdrawRefund`.

Also:
- In site/chain.js, send the native bid with an explicit `gas` (for example 400,000), as `deliverSymbols` already does, so wallets do not sign a tight estimate.
- Add a regression test with a mode-switching receiver that asserts the minimum gas for a successful bid is the same in cheap and burning modes.
- Record the change under K-09 in AUDIT.md, since this path is in the code that entry says still needs a review round.

