The artist should decide what the 100-wallet gate is for before the contract is frozen.

**Smallest code change that makes the gate real** — hold a refundable deposit, so 100 registrations lock 1 ETH instead of recycling 0.01 ETH:

```solidity
mapping(address => uint256) public registrationDeposit;

function register() external payable nonReentrant {
    if (msg.value != REGISTRATION_BALANCE) revert IncorrectPayment();
    _register(msg.sender);            // drop the wallet.balance check
    registrationDeposit[msg.sender] = msg.value;
}

function withdrawRegistrationDeposit(address to) external nonReentrant {
    if (registrationCount != REGISTRATION_TARGET) revert RegistrationIncomplete();
    uint256 amount = registrationDeposit[msg.sender];
    if (amount == 0) revert NothingToWithdraw();
    registrationDeposit[msg.sender] = 0;
    _pay(to, amount);
}
```

This also needs:
- an escape so deposits are not stuck forever if 100 is never reached, for example withdraw allowed after `startsAt + N days`;
- deposits added to `liabilities()`;
- `registerFor` either removed or made payable by the sponsor.

A `tx.origin` or `code.length` check alone is not a fix; it only forces 100 separate transactions.

**Alternative that fixes the clock control instead** — add a fixed delay between the 100th registration and the first accepted bid. Store `uint64 unlockedAt` when the count reaches 100 in `_register`, add an immutable `biddingDelay`, and in `_handleBid`:

```solidity
if (block.timestamp < unlockedAt + biddingDelay) revert AuctionNotOpen();
```

**If the code stays as it is** — the gate is ceremony, so say so and plan for it:
- Add to docs/NATIVE-ETH.md and the site terms: "One party can complete all 100 registrations and place the opening bid in a single transaction the moment startsAt passes; registration gives no bidding right and no protection. Treat startsAt as the real opening time."
- Announce `startsAt` as the opening time and have the artist and collectors ready to bid then.
- Keep the sponsor relayer behind its own per-wallet and budget limits.

Separately, if a price floor matters, relax ERC20EnglishAuction.sol:106 to `config.reservePrice < REGISTRATION_BALANCE` so the reserve can be set above 0.01 ETH.

