poc.fix:
Three small changes, all outside the immutable contracts.

**1. Refuse on read gas in script/DeployKilim.s.sol `_checkRenderer`.** Add the ceilings as constants and measure the calls the script already makes:
```solidity
uint256 public constant MAX_MASTERPIECE_READ_GAS = 24_000_000;
uint256 public constant MAX_ARTWORK_READ_GAS = 36_000_000;
...
uint256 g = gasleft();
string memory one = r.masterpieceURI();
g -= gasleft();
if (g + 21_000 > MAX_MASTERPIECE_READ_GAS) revert Refused("1/1 read gas over the ceiling");
if (sha256(bytes(one)) != vm.parseJsonBytes32(s.golden, ".masterpieceURI")) revert Refused("1/1 differs from golden");
```
Do the same around one `artworkURI` call built from the manifest's `.worst.byChars` list at 16x16 (256 cells), refusing above `MAX_ARTWORK_READ_GAS`. The golden case alone is not the worst case.

**2. Pin the final set on chain 1.** Once the pack is final, add to `_requireLaunchSettings`:
```solidity
uint256 public constant LAUNCH_MOTIF_COUNT = 1024;
bytes32 public constant LAUNCH_GEOMETRY_HASH = 0x...; // from the final manifest
...
if (c.motifCount != LAUNCH_MOTIF_COUNT) revert Refused("mainnet launch value: motifCount");
if (c.geometryHash != LAUNCH_GEOMETRY_HASH) revert Refused("mainnet launch value: geometryHash");
```
Ideally pin `indexHash` and `pageHash` too. `deployStore` does not call `_requireLaunchSettings` today, so call the motif and hash part from `deployStore` as well; otherwise the wrong store is refused only after about 40M gas of chunks is already on chain. Add matching cases to `testMainnetRefusesEverySettingOtherThanTheLaunchValues`.

**3. Change the site in the same commit as the final pack.** Update `MOTIFS` in site/chain.js:12 and the literal 812 in contracts/scripts/site-config.mjs:53. Better, have both read the count from one generated value (the manifest's `motifCount`) so they cannot drift.

**Before any of this:** the 1,024 set on disk (`onchain/current-1024`, KLC1, 1.22 MB) cannot be read by the current KLM1 renderer. It has to be repacked into a deployable store and pass RenderGasLimits before a mainnet config is signed off.

findings.description:
The reviewer wrapped shared behaviours in `address(paymentToken) == address(0)` so that only the launch mode changes. Twelve of sixteen such mutants survive all 232 tests:
- registered wallets may bid before the 100th registration (the gate at :217 is only tested with an unregistered bidder);
- settle() sweeps address(this).balance into proceedsDue, so the treasury takes other bidders' deferred refunds;
- a second deferred refund overwrites the first instead of adding to it;
- the anti-snipe extension is disabled;
- bids are accepted after endsAt;
- settle() is allowed before endsAt;
- the increment is ignored;
- non-0.001-ETH bids are accepted;
- the treasury may bid;
- claimPrize is open to anyone;
- the prize is not pushed at settlement.

The twelfth survivor is the REFUND_GAS lower bound, covered in F-05.

These paths are shared with ERC-20 mode and the ERC-20 tests do cover them, so this is not a bug in the on-disk code. The reviewer's scratch ETH-mode invariant run also held. But the ETH tests never settle with a deferred refund outstanding, never defer twice to one wallet, never bid inside the extension window, never settle to a contract winner and never call claimPrize. AuctionInvariants.t.sol runs only with MockUSD.

